        <title>Finite Tensor 2-Categories</title>
            <categories>math.CT math.QA</categories>
            <comments>39 pages, comments welcome!</comments>
            <report-no>MPIM-Bonn-2026</report-no>
            <msc-class>18N10, 18M05, 18M20, 16D90</msc-class>
            <license>http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/</license>
            <abstract>We propose a definition of a finite linear 2-category, as a 2-categorical analogue of the notion of a finite abelian category of Etingof-Ostrik. We go on to prove that finite linear 2-categories with adjunctible projectives are precisely the Morita 2-categories of (all) algebras in a finite multitensor category. Thus, finite linear 2-categories with adjunctible projectives can be viewed as `non-semisimple&#39; generalizations of the finite semisimple 2-categories of Douglas-Reutter.
  Secondly, we study finite multitensor 2-categories, that is, finite linear 2-categories equipped with a monoidal structure for which every objects has duals. We extend several results about fusion 2-categories to our present setting. In particular, we investigate the properties of the 2-category of bimodules over a rigid algebra $\mathcal{A}$ in a finite tensor 2-category $\mathfrak{C}$. We show that, if $\mathfrak{C}$ has adjunctible projectives, then the 2-category of $\mathcal{A}$-$\mathcal{A}$-bimodules in $\mathfrak{C}$ is a finite multitensor 2-category. This construction provides many examples of finite tensor 2-categories. For instance, the Drinfeld center of a finite tensor 2-category with adjunctible projectives is a finite tensor 2-category.</abstract>
